    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d73">

                <pb facs="0144" n="52" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg52"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the President</hi><anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d73-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-10-29">29 October 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For the President from Hull.</p>
                <p>Your Oct 28th<anchor n="2" xml:id="d73-f2"/> just received. I have been kept here
                    longer than I had expected and will not be able to leave before the 31st. Under
                    most favorable conditions I would not reach Washington prior to the 11th or
                    12th.</p>
                <p>I shall be glad to meet you on this side of the Atlantic at any time or place
                    that will suit your convenience.</p>
                <p>I have increasing indications that the Marshal will not go beyond Teheran. I
                    doubt seriously whether Molotov not being a military <pb facs="0145" n="53"
                        xml:id="pg53"/> man would be sent as substitute. Without his knowledge of my
                    purpose I sounded him out indirectly.</p>
                <p>I will continue to press the Stalin matter and Harriman will after I leave.</p>
                <p>Wire me at Teheran and Cairo as to where you desire me to meet you.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d73-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d73-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to Washington by the United States Naval Attach, Moscow, via Navy channels,
                    and forwarded by the White House Map Room to Roosevelt, who was at Hyde Park
                    October 30–November 3, 1943.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d73-f2" n="2" xml:id="d73-f2-content">
